Hi, <div><br></div><div>I noticed different behaviors between v0.2.3 and v0.2.4 when using uiOutput. See my code below. </div><div>I tested the exact same code on 2 machines with the following sessionInfo:</div><div><b>Machine 1: IT WORKS !!</b></div><div><div>R version 2.15.1 (2012-06-22)</div><div>Platform: x86_64-pc-linux-gnu (64-bit)</div><div><br></div><div>locale:</div><div> [1] LC_CTYPE=en_US.UTF-8       LC_NUMERIC=C              </div><div> [3] LC_TIME=en_US.UTF-8        LC_COLLATE=en_US.UTF-8    </div><div> [5] LC_MONETARY=en_US.UTF-8    LC_MESSAGES=en_US.UTF-8   </div><div> [7] LC_PAPER=C                 LC_NAME=C                 </div><div> [9] LC_ADDRESS=C               LC_TELEPHONE=C            </div><div>[11] LC_MEASUREMENT=en_US.UTF-8 LC_IDENTIFICATION=C       </div><div><br></div><div>attached base packages:</div><div>[1] stats     graphics  grDevices utils     datasets  methods   base     </div><div><br></div><div>other attached packages:</div><div>[1] shiny_0.2.3</div><div><br></div><div>loaded via a namespace (and not attached):</div><div>[1] bitops_1.0-5     caTools_1.13     digest_0.6.0     RJSONIO_1.0-1   </div><div>[5] websockets_1.1.6 xtable_1.7-0 </div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><b>Machine 2: IT DOES NOT WORK with the error message: <font color="#ff0000">$ operator is invalid for atomic vectors</font></b></div><div>R version 2.15.2 (2012-10-26)<br></div><div><div>Platform: i486-pc-linux-gnu (32-bit)</div><div><br></div><div>locale:</div><div> [1] LC_CTYPE=fr_BE.UTF-8       LC_NUMERIC=C              </div><div> [3] LC_TIME=fr_BE.UTF-8        LC_COLLATE=fr_BE.UTF-8    </div><div> [5] LC_MONETARY=fr_BE.UTF-8    LC_MESSAGES=fr_BE.UTF-8   </div><div> [7] LC_PAPER=C                 LC_NAME=C                 </div><div> [9] LC_ADDRESS=C               LC_TELEPHONE=C            </div><div>[11] LC_MEASUREMENT=fr_BE.UTF-8 LC_IDENTIFICATION=C       </div><div><br></div><div>attached base packages:</div><div>[1] stats     graphics  grDevices utils     datasets  methods   base     </div><div><br></div><div>other attached packages:</div><div>[1] shiny_0.2.4</div><div><br></div><div>loaded via a namespace (and not attached):</div><div>[1] bitops_1.0-4.1   caTools_1.13     digest_0.5.2     RJSONIO_1.0-1   </div><div>[5] websockets_1.1.6 xtable_1.7-0 </div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>What should I do to make it running with shiny_0.2.4? Thanks in advance for your help. </div><div><br></div><div>JB <br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><b>ui.R </b></div><div><div>library(shiny)</div><div><br></div><div>shinyUI(</div><div>  pageWithSidebar(</div><div>    headerPanel(&quot;QP Bioinfo Pipeline&quot;),</div><div>    sidebarPanel(</div><div>      radioButtons(&#39;test&#39;, &#39;My test&#39;,</div><div>                   c(&#39;1&#39;=&#39;1&#39;,</div><div>                     &#39;2&#39;=&#39;2&#39;),</div><div>                   &#39;1&#39;)</div><div>      ),</div><div>    mainPanel(</div><div>      uiOutput(&quot;tableUI&quot;)</div><div>      )</div><div>    )</div><div>  )</div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><b>server.R</b></div><div><div>library(shiny)</div><div><br></div><div>shinyServer(function(input, output) {</div><div><br></div><div>  output$tableUI &lt;- reactiveUI(function(){</div><div>    myhtml&lt;-&quot;&lt;!-- html table generated in R 2.15.2 by xtable 1.7-0 package --&gt;
&lt;!-- Thu Dec 27 00:05:04 2012 --&gt;
&lt;TABLE border=1&gt;
&lt;TR&gt; &lt;TH&gt; Include? &lt;/TH&gt; &lt;TH&gt; varname &lt;/TH&gt; &lt;TH&gt; firstVar &lt;/TH&gt; &lt;/TR&gt;
  &lt;TR&gt;\</div><div>  &lt;TD class=\&quot;ui-helper-center\&quot;&gt;&lt;label class=\&quot;checkbox\&quot;&gt;
   &lt;input id=\&quot;row_1\&quot; type=\&quot;checkbox\&quot; checked=\&quot;checked\&quot;/&gt;
   
&lt;/label&gt; &lt;/TD&gt; &lt;TD&gt; row_1 &lt;/TD&gt; &lt;TD&gt; firstVarValue &lt;/TD&gt; &lt;/TR&gt;
   &lt;/TABLE&gt;&quot;</div><div>    return(myhtml)</div><div>  })</div><div>})</div></div><div><br></div><div><br></div>
